{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_95","type":"agent_message","text":"Created [solution_4.py](/root/solution_4.py).\n\nIt uses TensorCircuit’s density-matrix simulator (`DMCircuit2`) with the custom asymmetric bit-flip Kraus channel inserted after each entangler layer, generates the synthetic target table from the true probabilities, and runs exactly 120 Adam updates with JAX automatic differentiation. All 13 observables per probe are obtained in one tensor-network contraction.\n\nVerified against the default config:\n\n- Runtime: ~6.4 s\n- `loss_history` length: 120\n- Final probabilities: `[0.034030, 0.011014]`\n- Absolute parameter errors: `[3.0e-5, 1.4e-5]`\n- Kraus trace-preserving error: ~1e-16\n- `fitted_expectations` shape: `(4, 13)`"}}
